# A data segment that is not acknowledged is retransmitted with a
# timestamp option like every other segment: the current TSval, and the
# TSecr of the handshake's last ACK.  The handshake gave an RTT sample of
# 100 ms (its TSecr), so the RTO is 100 + 200 ms.  The first resend is
# the tail loss probe, due at 2 * SRTT + 200 ms (one segment out) but
# never later than the RTO: at 0.6; the RTO then counts from the probe
# (0.9), doubling after it (1.5).
# Copyright (C) 2026 The LikeOS Project
tolerance 20
0.000 socket s stream
0.000 bind s 8080
0.000 listen s 16
0.100 < S 0:0(0) win 65535 <mss 1460,sackOK,TS val 100 ecr 0,nop,wscale 7>
0.100 > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win * <mss 1460,sackOK,TS val * ecr 100,nop,wscale *>
0.200 < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 512 <nop,nop,TS val 200 ecr echo>
0.200 accept s c
0.300 send c 100 = 100
0.300 > P. 1:101(100) ack 1 win * <nop,nop,TS val ~ ecr 200>
0.600 > P. 1:101(100) ack 1 win * <nop,nop,TS val ~ ecr 200>
0.900 > P. 1:101(100) ack 1 win * <nop,nop,TS val ~ ecr 200>
1.500 > P. 1:101(100) ack 1 win * <nop,nop,TS val ~ ecr 200>
1.510 < . 1:1(0) ack 101 win 512 <nop,nop,TS val 1510 ecr echo>
